# WEBrick logged whatever it is handed: BasicLog#format returned
# arg.message and arg.to_str verbatim, and every string that reached a
# logger call went to the log device with its control characters intact
# (CWE-117). The exploitable flow is HTTP Basic authentication, where a
# username decoded straight from the Authorization header is interpolated
# into an error message:
#
#   lib/webrick/httpauth/basicauth.rb
#     userid, password = basic_credentials.unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)
#     unless encpass = @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, @reload_db)
#       error("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
#
# and the Authenticator module turns that into a log write:
#
#   lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
#     def log(meth, fmt, *args)
#       msg = format("%s %s: ", @auth_scheme, @realm)
#       msg << fmt % args
#       @logger.send(meth, msg)
#     end
#
# The fixed revision wraps both branches of BasicLog#format in AccessLog.escape and
# removes the older escape from HTTPStatus::Status#initialize, so escaping
# now happens once, at the log boundary, for plain strings as well as
# exceptions. The regression test drives a "foo\ebar" username and asserts
# the log carries no escape sequence.
#
# ATTENTION, and the miss is structural in two independent places. The rule
# that should fire is VYQL-INJ-009 (taint core.UserControlledData ->
# code.LogOutput unless core.LogEscape), and its Ruby sink bindings cover
# only the bare `logger.error` receiver spelling. WEBrick writes logs
# through `@logger.send(meth, msg)` (authenticator.rb) and `@log << data`
# (log.rb's BasicLog#log) -- dynamic Object#send dispatch on a
# config-injected object and an instance-variable device write, neither of
# which a binding can label without keying on a receiver's name, which is
# not a documented logging API. A probe widening of @logger.info/warn/error/
# write is measured and reverted: across the whole 63-file tree it fired
# exactly one finding, filehandler.rb's `@logger.warn("the request refers
# nondisclosure name `#{File.basename(res.filename)}'.")`, identically at
# the vulnerable and the patched revision (the fixed revision does not touch that
# file), while adding 19 medium log-injection rows of ordinary
# `@logger.info("... #{env[:x]} ...")` operational logging on one
# 867-file subtree (97 to 116 findings).
#
# Even with a sink available, the flow dies one step earlier. The second
# and third snippets are a minimal pair over the message assembly itself:
# building the message as `msg = "prefix: " << fmt % args` reports
# VYQL-INJ-009 today, and building it as `msg = "prefix: "; msg << fmt %
# args` does not -- a self-mutating `<<` in statement position propagates
# nothing to its receiver, while the same call in expression position
# carries the argument's taint through its result. WEBrick uses the
# statement form. The neutraliser half is unreachable too: the fixed revision's
# AccessLog.escape is a `gsub(/[[:cntrl:]\\]+/)`, and a Ruby regex-literal
# argument is not exposed as an `args.any.literal` token, so logEscape342
# (`gsub` + literal contains "[[:cntrl:]]") cannot label it; the same call
# with a string pattern does label.
#
# The pair is recorded as the engine gap: statement-position `<<` needs a
# new receiver-mutation relation for every Ruby String/Array/IO append,
# which is not a mechanical correction, and the `send` sink behind it is a
# second blocker on the same path.

test "rank1944: the basic auth username reaches the log unescaped"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/basicauth.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def check_scheme(req)
          unless credentials = req[@request_field]
            error("no credentials in the request.")
            return nil
          end
          match = /^#{@auth_scheme}\s+/i.match(credentials)
          match.post_match
        end

        def error(fmt, *args)
          if @logger.error?
            log(:error, fmt, *args)
          end
        end

        def log(meth, fmt, *args)
          msg = format("%s %s: ", @auth_scheme, @realm)
          msg << fmt % args
          @logger.send(meth, msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate(req, res)
          unless basic_credentials = check_scheme(req)
            challenge(req, res)
          end
          userid, password = basic_credentials.unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)
          password ||= ""
          unless encpass = @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, @reload_db)
            error("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
            challenge(req, res)
          end
          req.user = userid
        end

        def challenge(req, res)
          raise Unauthorized
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the fixed revision escapes every logged value at the log boundary"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/log.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    class BasicLog
      def error(msg)
        log(ERROR, "ERROR " << format(msg))
      end

      def log(level, data)
        if @log && level <= @level
          data += "\n" if /\n\Z/ !~ data
          @log << data
        end
      end

      def format(arg)
        if arg.is_a?(Exception)
          "#{arg.class}: #{AccessLog.escape(arg.message)}\n\t" <<
          arg.backtrace.join("\n\t") << "\n"
        elsif arg.respond_to?(:to_str)
          AccessLog.escape(arg.to_str)
        else
          arg.inspect
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the message assembled in expression position is reported"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def log(fmt, *args)
          msg = "WEBrick's realm: " << fmt % args
          logger.error(msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate
          userid = params["authorization"].unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)[0]
          unless @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, true)
            log("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the same append in statement position loses the taint"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def log(fmt, *args)
          msg = "WEBrick's realm: "
          msg << fmt % args
          logger.error(msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate
          userid = params["authorization"].unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)[0]
          unless @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, true)
            log("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
